{"reference":"Proverbs 30","book":"Proverbs","chapter":30,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Distinct Voice in Proverbs","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The heading identifies these sayings with Agur son of Jakeh. Proverbs’ final chapters preserve distinct voices associated with Agur, King Lemuel, and Lemuel’s mother, alongside other named and unnamed collections in the book; they are not simply identified together as Solomon’s words. This helps readers receive Proverbs 30 as a collection with its own introduced speaker and voice.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 30:1","Proverbs 30:1-33"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_030_f905003deeae820dad100481"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}